   (SECOTOX) Conference, GREECE, JUN 19-24, 2011},
Organization = {Int Soc Ecotoxicol \& Environm Safety; Univ Thessaly, Dept Planning \&
   Reg Dev; Aristotle Univ Thessaloniki, Dept Mech Engn; Natl Tech Univ
   Athens, Sch Mech Engn, Sect Ind Management \& Operat Res; TEI W
   Macedonia, Dept Pollut Control Technologies},
Abstract = {The island of Rhodes is one of the most popular tourist destinations in
   Greece. However, the lack of tourism development planning has led to an
   overexploitation of resources and to gradual environmental degradation.
   The aim of this paper is to present a set of proposals concerning the
   sustainable development of the island. A general analysis of the area
   was carried out and specific problems and opportunities were identified
   through a SWOT (Strengths - Weaknesses - Opportunities - Threats)
   analysis of the region. Public participation was also incorporated into
   the whole process through a questionnaire survey, which investigated
   public opinions and perceptions concerning the existing problems and
   development opportunities on the island of Rhodes. After combining the
   SWOT analysis and the survey results, a general framework of proposals
   was formulated and further evaluated by an expert group through pairwise
   comparisons. The final out-come of the whole process is a portfolio of
   proposals, projects, activities, constructions and actions that need to
   be effectively implemented in order to target the sustainable
   development of this coastal area.},
