   Management; German Acad Exchange Serv Fdn; German Ind \& Commerce; Off
   European Commiss Hong Kong \& Macao; CSR Asia},
Abstract = {In this article, the author establishes a system dynamic model to carry
   on simulation for the traditional development mode and circular economic
   mode in Shenzhen up to the Year 2030. The simulation shows that the GDP
   and population of the city will increase remarkably in 2020 by following
   circular economic development mode. In addition, water shortage and
   environmental problems will be partially solved due to the
   implementation of the circular mode. Suggestions for water saving as
   well as population and pollution control are provided at the end of the
   paper based on the results from the simulation.},
