Number = {6, SI},
Pages = {1662-1665},
Month = {JUN},
Note = {International Conference on Business, Management, Tourism and
   Hospitality (BIZMATOUR), Malacca, MALAYSIA, MAY 12-14, 2015},
Abstract = {Competency models are often used in organizations as a tool to identify
   and describe knowledge, skills, abilities, personal characteristics and
   behavior necessary for workers to perform effectively. This paper
   discusses the findings of a need assessment study which has been
   conducted in order to identify the perceptions of job incumbents in the
   culinary industry regarding the development of a competency model for
   the profession. A total of 42 respondents were involved in the study.
   The analysis indicated that the needs for the development of a
   competency model for culinary profession named as the Culinary
   Competency Model are supported. A qualitative data collection by means
   of interviews was conducted to support the analysis of the questionnaire
   data. The findings show that there is a need to develop a competency
   model exclusively for culinary profession. A competency model that
   addresses specific competencies is essential as career guidance for
   people in the profession. Furthermore, several insights on the
   directions for future research are included in this article after
   examining the results from the needs assessment.},
