Note = {8th National Conference on Thermophysical Properties (NCTP), Jaipur,
   INDIA, DEC 14-16, 2015},
Abstract = {Information literacy education is increasingly becoming essential as
   information technology turns out to be an integral part of daily life.
   Even the lives of elderly people are not exempted by the changes brought
   about by technological innovations in the society. In fact, in the
   information society, the participation of elderly people through the
   on-line is important for the regional development and innovation. With
   this trend, this study concentrated on the information literacy
   education and investigated the impact of information literacy education
   in developing innovative thinking and changing perceptions of elderly
   Korean group. This study utilized both face to face interview and online
   survey to gather responses from Koreans who are over 50 years of age
   living in different residential areas of South Korea. The total 640
   usual questionnaires are collected and analyzed. The result indicated
   that elderly people who participated in the information literacy
   education reflected more innovative attitude and manifested a positive
   change in their outlook in life. In addition, innovativeness differences
   by gender, age, and residential area were analyzed. The implications of
   these findings and recommendations were also discussed.},
