   KOREA, AUG 25-29, 2024},
Abstract = {This paper is about how visual elements in paper packaging impacts
   users. The purpose of this study is to examine how visual components
   influence the perceptions and preferences of Buyers for Indian
   paper/plastic packaging Design. Tea and bottled juice products are given
   special attention in this study so as to investigate how features like
   image/pattern, colour/typeface and shape have an impact on consumers'
   choices. An online survey was conducted with 105 respondents aged
   between 18-30 years who were shown images of three different brand's
   teas as well as three others having juices in bottles while rating them
   according to their likeness and the relevance levels of each visual
   element (colour; image/pattern; typeface) also using a Likert scale.
   From this standpoint, visual elements need to be tactically thought out
   when it comes to making paper packaging designs for any market. Colour
   is essential but depending on the category of commodities; shape on its
   part may also matter while pattern plays different roles too.},
