   together Engineering and Economics (ICEE), Guimaraes, PORTUGAL, MAY
   16-17, 2019},
Organization = {Univ Minho, Sch Engn; Univ Porto, Sch Econ \& Management; UP, Ctr Econ
   \& Finance; CentroAlgoritmi},
Abstract = {The residential photovoltaic (PV) self-consumption allows households to
   consume the energy produced through their solar panels. This paradigm
   shift in the electric system, placing the households as producers, can
   be important to boost their energy awareness. The environmental and
   energy perception of prosumers (i.e. simultaneously producers and
   consumers) is expected to change with the transition to a low carbon
   system, as their energy consumption patterns will contribute to smooth
   the electricity load diagram. Thus, it is necessary to understand which
   are the main factors that stimulate this shift. This paper studies this
   behaviour changes in energy consumption, based on primary data
   collection through a survey in Portugal, using an Ordered Logit
   Regressions. This paper proves that the awareness of prosumers in
   relation to energy consumption increases after PV self-consumption and
   that they are more available to change their peak consumption time to
   take advantage from the solar prodution, thus smoothing their
   electricity load diagram. Technology can help with this issue. In fact,
   the probability of increasing the load shifting with remote control is
   50\% and with monitoring system is 42\%.},
