Note = {22nd Congress of the International Ergonomics Association-IEA, SOUTH
   KOREA, AUG 25-29, 2024},
Abstract = {Objective: To identify risk factors for musculoskeletal disorders (MSD)
   in the reception of meat products in slaughterhouses. Methods:
   Descriptive, cross-sectional, observational study with a mixed approach,
   with activity analysis, in a company with dispatch centers.
   Participants: The analysis is carried out in 4 cities, based on the
   ergonomic analysis of the work activity, in each of which the supervisor
   and the personnel performing the removal tasks participate. Observation
   and interviews: Observations were carried out in two days, completely.
   Photographs and films were taken with a Sony Hybrid 25x camera and
   analyzed with tumeke software. Interviews were conducted directly with
   the workers to learn about their perception of the work and to
   investigate with them possible improvements. Biomechanical risk:
   analyzed with Tumeke software to analyze each segment and the risk in
   the different tasks for which videos were available. Results: The risks
   of manual handling of loads, pushing and pulling actions in this type of
   tasks are very demanding and the intervention should be aimed at
   improving working con-ditions based on engineering proposals.},
