   Sci Romanian Acad},
Abstract = {Infrastructure is a complex facility that provides resources, and
   related scientific services used by scientists for fundamental and
   applied research, fostering innovation. All research infrastructures
   were put to a test during the COVID-19 pandemic across the world. The
   aim of this study was to evaluate the impact of the COVID-19 pandemic on
   the Romanian research infrastructure. A questionnaire was developed and
   sent to the Romanian RDIIs (Research, Development and Innovation
   Infrastructure) to understand the pandemic's impact on the
   organizations. The pandemic has not influenced the performance of the
   Romanian RDIIs, nor created difficulties in maintaining existing
   customers, identifying new opportunities to access funds, or identifying
   project implementation. For the RDIIs participating in this survey, the
   COVID-19 pandemic has not impacted financial growth or staff retention
   but has created difficulties in finding partners/clients for particular
   research projects. Unfortunately, due to a limited eligible population,
   the reported results strictly reflect the respondents' perception and
   cannot be generalized, hence, no recommendations can be made based on
   the reported results.},
