Note = {2nd International Research Conference on Business and Economics (IRCBE),
   Semarang, INDONESIA, AUG 03-04, 2016},
Abstract = {Recognising the important role of entrepreneurs and SMEs in the economy,
   this paper employed qualitative study to understand the perception of
   Malaysian SMEs entrepreneurs regarding the concept of sustainability,
   creativity and innovation. Fifty-six sole entrepreneurs of SMEs in
   Malaysia from various business activities are chosen as respondents. The
   findings discovered important key phrases under the theme creativity and
   innovation where most respondents viewed this element as diversification
   of product or services technology application, utilising premium
   materials and ingredient, creating new ideas and the improvement of
   existing products. However, self-improvement, motivation or support,
   entrepreneur's attitude/behaviour and good relationship with supply
   chain or networking are among the respondents' interpretation of
   sustainability. The findings from this study is anticipated to
   contribute literatures on entrepreneurship study whilst assisting
   entrepreneurs and SMEs to identify and apply the concept of creativity
   and innovation and find the aspect to sustain in the business.
   Nevertheless, this study also has some limitations in terms of the
   number of respondents which may be insufficient to represent all SMEs
   entrepreneurs in Malaysia.},
