Pages = {359+},
Note = {10th International Conference on the Mediterranean Coastal Environment,
   Rhodes, GREECE, OCT 25-29, 2011},
Organization = {Mediterranean Coastal Fdn; Hellenic Republ, S Aegean Reg; Municipal
   Rhodes; UNEP, Mediterranean Act Plan},
Abstract = {Coastal managers together with planners need coastal landscape
   inventories in order to base sound management decisions on ascertained
   facts. Coastal areas are under threat due to the forcing function of
   people who flock to the coast for habitation and/or recreation, which
   affects a strategic asset coastal scenery. In this paper, many coastal
   scenery parameters, obtained from a literature search/questionnaires
   (>800), were subsequently pared to 26. Parameter preferences and
   priorities obtained by perception studies were weighted pre fuzzy logic
   analysis via matrices relating to the selected landscape components.
   Beaches on Hong Kong Island are sparse in number and coastal scenery
   values were investigated at five Hong Kong island beaches chosen to
   represent the main recreational beaches. An Evaluation Decision Index
   (D) value enabled scenic differentiation. Class 1 scenery, had D values
   > 0.85; Class 2, between 0.85 and 0.65; Class 3, between 0.65 and 0.4;
   Class 4, between 0.4 and zero; Class 5, below zero. The D values found
   varied from 0.04 to 0.96.},
