   Hong Kong Inst Util Specialists},
Abstract = {Several car manufacturers have proposed an alternative mode of auto
   transport called the low speed private travel mode (LSPTM). It is a
   small single-seat electric vehicle that can run at speeds of around 5-20
   km/h. Further, it is regarded as a tool to improve the mobility of
   pedestrians and encourage the use of public transport. The aim of this
   study was to estimate how the mobility of pedestrians will be improved
   and how the environment will be impacted by the introduction of this
   vehicle. At the outset, a stated preference survey is conducted to
   ascertain the users' preference for the LSPTM to walking based on the
   actual trips of the respondents measured using the probe person survey
   system. To evaluate how traveller's activities will be expanded by the
   LSPTM, a joint logit model was constructed to describe the destination
   and mode choices of travellers in the central area of Kobe. Based on the
   model, it was concluded that the size of the area where half the number
   of people visit increased by 2.6 times after introducing the LSPTM at a
   fare of 50 yen. The environmental impact of the LSPTM was also assessed.},
