   Management; German Acad Exchange Serv Fdn; German Ind \& Commerce; Off
   European Commiss Hong Kong \& Macao; CSR Asia},
Abstract = {Research shows that rainwater harvesting may be an accessible approach
   to solve water resources scarcity in the and and semi-arid regions in
   northern China. However, only roof-yard catchments systems can collect
   the qualified rainwater that meets the international standards for
   drinking water. By analysis of the water samples taken from the
   different rainwater cisterns, the author finds out that Faecal Coliform
   tremendously exceeded the drinking water standard while rainwater
   quality that was significantly affected by the different catchments
   systems which contain different organic micro-pollutants. In comparison
   of a number of disinfectants for drinking water disinfection, chlorine
   dioxide, as the most feasible and effective oxidant was finally selected
   to use. However, the function of chlorine dioxide is greatly affected by
   the wayClO(2)are added and pH value of treated water. This paper
   introduces a new chlorine dioxide (ClO2) generator with the reaction of
   sodium chloride, sulfuric acid and soluble starch.},
