   Algarve, PORTUGAL, APR 25-27, 2007},
Organization = {Wessex Inst Technol; Univ Thessaly; WIT Transact Built Environm; ASCE UK
   Int Grp},
Abstract = {This paper investigates the impact of cultural goods on the housing
   market considering environmental factors related to tourism in an
   Italian city. In the first section, the willingness to pay for cultural
   goods is estimated by using the hedonic pricing model for the commercial
   property (tourism). In this regression, the link between environmental
   factors and the number of tourists is studied, which in turn quantifies
   the prospects for `sustainable' or at least environmentally friendly
   tourism. On the basis of the results further questions are posed, e.g.,
   whether tourism increases social welfare for local residents - also in
   conjunction with public policy.},
