   RENNES, FRANCE, JUN 06-10, 1993},
Organization = {INT ASSOC LANDSCAPE ECOL},
Abstract = {In the Netherlands the increasing demand for hydro-ecological models on
   a regional (provincial) scale, resulted in the development of an
   empirical impact-assessment model for terrestrial ecosystems.  The model
   describes the relationship between plant species and site factors such
   as soil, groundwater and management.  Seasonal dynamics are implemented
   in the model and much attention is paid to the chemistry of water and
   soil.  The model is developed for the region of the province of
   Noord-Holland and will be applied to support provincial soil and water
   management.},
