   and Health Engineering (WEESHE), SEOUL NATL UNIV, SEOUL, SOUTH KOREA,
   OCT 18-21, 1999},
Organization = {Seoul Natl Univ; Louisiana State Univ; Korean Soc Civil Engineers; Korea
   Water Resources Assoc; Korean Soc Water \& Waste Water; Korean Soc Agr
   Engn},
Abstract = {Clogging phenomenon is one of the: most serious problems in operating
   underground storage caverns of hydrocarbon. To prevent clogging
   phenomena, injection water quality is very important. This experimental
   study describes clogging phenomena caused by accumulation of dissolved
   hydrocarbons to determine the criteria of injection water quality for an
   efficient operation of the storage cavern. Injection tests are performed
   with an artificially fractured granite core using injection water
   containing hydrocarbons. This study shows that clogging occurs in case
   the difference of solubility exists, and the degree of clogging depend
   on operating conditions such as temperature, operating pressure, etc.
   The results of this study can be applied to determine the criteria of
   injection water quality for recycling of the seepage water in
   underground storage caverns, and it can contribute to reducing the
   treatment cost of the injection water and conserving water resources.},
